    "coachNote": "Atomic numbers are number facts. The game's own Major pictures (the \"majorWord\" field, from the default list) give each number a picture to join to the element picture: iron is 26, \"notch\", an iron nail in a notch. Use it for the numbers you keep losing. The pattern of the table (rows, groups) is learned by understanding, not by pictures.",
    "honest": "This is memorising names and numbers for a class or for fun. It does not teach chemistry. Keep the table open next to it when you study the real subject.",
